    "type": "game",
    "name": "Catastrophic Inversion",
    "steam_appid": 3620680,
    "required_age": 0,
    "is_free": false,
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Catastrophic Inversion</strong> is a multiplayer VR shooter made for <strong>large shared spaces</strong>, allowing players to naturally move among each other in massive levels with space-warping tricks to make them feel even bigger.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Combatants face off in a variety of game modes including <strong>Capture-The-Flag</strong>, <strong>Deathmatch</strong>, and <strong>Elimination</strong>, with many adjustable settings. You can also mix and match win states to create your own custom modes.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Teleport and Joystick Locomotion</strong> are also available for those who don't have a large playspace available.</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>PCVR has only been tested on Meta AirLink</strong> and might only work on Meta headsets. Currently the native Meta Quest edition looks and runs slightly cleaner than the PCVR edition. </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Cross-play is available between Meta Quest and Steam, as well as between stationary and real-space players. <i>(We are aware that most PCVR players do not have a fully-mobile setup.)</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>This PC edition can also function as a dedicated server</strong> <strong>and a spectator camera</strong> for those not currently playing. If the game starts without a headset connected, it will automatically enter server/spectator mode.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game can be played <strong>completely offline</strong> via a local Wi-Fi network, or <strong>online through</strong> a direct connection to <strong>privately hosted servers</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>While fully-playable as an arena shooter, we still have a lot planned. We are working on adding arenas, weapons, items, play styles, accessibility options, and quality-of-life features.</i></p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Catastrophic Inversion</strong> is a multiplayer VR shooter made for <strong>large shared spaces</strong>, allowing players to naturally move among each other in massive levels with space-warping tricks to make them feel even bigger.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Combatants face off in a variety of game modes including <strong>Capture-The-Flag</strong>, <strong>Deathmatch</strong>, and <strong>Elimination</strong>, with many adjustable settings. You can also mix and match win states to create your own custom modes.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Teleport and Joystick Locomotion</strong> are also available for those who don't have a large playspace available.</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>PCVR has only been tested on Meta AirLink</strong> and might only work on Meta headsets. Currently the native Meta Quest edition looks and runs slightly cleaner than the PCVR edition. </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Cross-play is available between Meta Quest and Steam, as well as between stationary and real-space players. <i>(We are aware that most PCVR players do not have a fully-mobile setup.)</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>This PC edition can also function as a dedicated server</strong> <strong>and a spectator camera</strong> for those not currently playing. If the game starts without a headset connected, it will automatically enter server/spectator mode.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game can be played <strong>completely offline</strong> via a local Wi-Fi network, or <strong>online through</strong> a direct connection to <strong>privately hosted servers</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>While fully-playable as an arena shooter, we still have a lot planned. We are working on adding arenas, weapons, items, play styles, accessibility options, and quality-of-life features.</i></p>",
    "short_description": "Catastrophic Inversion is a VR shooter made for large shared spaces using real movement through space-warping, multi-story arenas. Join cross-platform with Meta Quest from stationary VR or join in real space if you have a portable PCVR device. This also acts as a dedicated server and spectator.",
    "supported_languages": "English<strong>*</strong><br><strong>*</strong>languages with full audio support",
